# Custom HTTP headers for GitHub Pages.
#
# GitHub Pages serves files by extension; `.ttl` already maps to
# "text/turtle; charset=utf-8" on the live site (measured), but an
# extensionless file gets a generic type. `vocab/0.2.0` is the exact
# target of `owl:versionIRI` in `vocab.ttl`, so it must be served with the
# RDF media type like its `.ttl` sibling. Paths below are relative to the
# site root — GitHub Pages serves this repo under the project base path
# `/web/` itself, so the rule must not repeat that prefix; the web owner
# with deploy rights confirms the actual response header after this lands
# (this lane cannot deploy per its brief).

/vocab/0.2.0
  Content-Type: text/turtle; charset=utf-8
